<title>ITALY: Italian crude imports up 0.6 pct in Jan/Feb 1997.</title>
<headline>Italian crude imports up 0.6 pct in Jan/Feb 1997.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian imports of crude oil amounted to some 12.7 million tonnes in January and February 1997, up 0.6 percent on the same 1996 period, industry association Unione Petrolifera said in a statement.</p>
<p>Libya supplied 29.3 percent of Italian crude imports, Saudi Arabia 17.4 percent, Iran 14.4 percent and the former Soviet Union 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>UP said data for the first quarter of 1997 showed that the cost of imported crude, equal to 256,900 lire per tonne, showed an increase of 19.0 percent over the same 1996 period.</p>
<p>This was due to 14.8 percent higher crude prices in dollar terms and a 3.6 percent appreciation of the U.S. currency against the lira.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
